\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Equal arcs and the quadratic content}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Partition the circle of \ref{fdip-00BG} into #{N\ge 2} arcs
of length #{1/N}. Inside one arc the shorter distance is at
most #{1/N}, so \ref{fdip-00D2} bounds the diameter in the
[increment metric](fdip-00CY) by #{N^{-1/2}}. The sum of the
squares of these diameters is at most #{1}. The
[Hausdorff content](fdip-00D5) of order #{2} is therefore at
most #{1}.}
